{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012SdXpV26f4Z9g91uPChM7W","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are not directly available in the search results. However, I can share what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning, and CoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Related Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions to CoRL 2026 must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Previous CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile the specific 2026 guidelines weren't available in the search results, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines indicate that reviews should evaluate whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website or OpenReview submission system directly, as the detailed review forms and guidelines may not yet be publicly available this early in the submission process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"8e7859d8-61bd-4e9a-a8fe-70e867dc781e","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:18:28.971Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JBKMFPCveMh4RMdA5JsXJz","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form details are not directly available in the search results. However, I can share what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL is an annual international conference focusing on the intersection of robotics and machine learning, and CoRL 2026 will be held in Austin, Texas, US.\n\n## Related Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions to CoRL 2026 must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer and is qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ ICRA/ IROS/ RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/ NeurIPS/ ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n## Previous CoRL Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile the specific 2026 guidelines weren't available in the search results, the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines indicate that reviews should evaluate whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method or learned model, whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested in reading the paper.\n\nFor the most current and complete CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website or OpenReview submission system directly, as the detailed review forms and guidelines may not yet be publicly available this early in the submission process."],"durationSeconds":6.120104942000002}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L9TATPNMzVktc3YwaWXewZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck\",\"url\":\"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning), though the specific 2025 reviewer guidelines document wasn't directly returned. Here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines:**\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, and judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as relevance to robotic learning.\n\nReviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences like CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, and core machine learning venues like NeurIPS and ICML.\n\n**Regarding acceptance rate:** The search results do not contain specific information about the CoRL 2025 acceptance rate or detailed scoring criteria. The most recent reference (a Speaker Deck presentation from October 2025) mentions that CoRL 2025 had a participation scale and acceptance rate overview, but the specific numbers weren't included in the search results.\n\nFor the most detailed and official CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and acceptance rate information, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"945377bd-3bf4-4630-807b-60e609af1a32","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:18:30.065Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring criteria acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01P66vBqi6j7Xyb1HZEZbmxt","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck","url":"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning), though the specific 2025 reviewer guidelines document wasn't directly returned. Here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines:**\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results, and judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as relevance to robotic learning.\n\nReviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences like CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, and core machine learning venues like NeurIPS and ICML.\n\n**Regarding acceptance rate:** The search results do not contain specific information about the CoRL 2025 acceptance rate or detailed scoring criteria. The most recent reference (a Speaker Deck presentation from October 2025) mentions that CoRL 2025 had a participation scale and acceptance rate overview, but the specific numbers weren't included in the search results.\n\nFor the most detailed and official CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, scoring criteria, and acceptance rate information, I'd recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website directly."],"durationSeconds":6.763518947999999}}
