{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013iyKG4B6vFCa1bTPCjcBD8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024\"},{\"title\":\"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up\",\"url\":\"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found about the review criteria:\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results show the main review criteria page for CoRL 2024, but the specific scoring scale and rating criteria details appear to be truncated in the search results. The page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews contains the full instructions for reviewers, but the complete scoring scale information is not fully visible in the excerpt provided.\n\nTo see the complete scoring scale and all rating criteria, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page directly at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"14678fce-cb86-49c4-b909-ec0f604dd011","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:18:43.141Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HXhRgXAHKDoGKdjxbr9xGo","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL.2024 | Cool Papers - Immersive Paper Discovery","url":"https://papers.cool/venue/CoRL.2024"},{"title":"Game Review Scoring Systems: Complete Rating Guide 2024 – Ofoxil Level-Up","url":"https://ofoxil.net/game-review-scoring-systems-complete-rating-guide-2024/"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page. Here's what I found about the review criteria:\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nThe search results show the main review criteria page for CoRL 2024, but the specific scoring scale and rating criteria details appear to be truncated in the search results. The page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews contains the full instructions for reviewers, but the complete scoring scale information is not fully visible in the excerpt provided.\n\nTo see the complete scoring scale and all rating criteria, I recommend visiting the official CoRL 2024 Instruction for Reviews page directly at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"],"durationSeconds":5.6686658959999985}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011xSWSvEseiotxVNptGXVES","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines review form questions rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965318/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965317/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines and review form questions:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe specific review form questions include:\n\n1. **Originality**: Whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n2. **Quality**: Whether the submission is technically sound, claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, methods are appropriate, whether it is complete work or work in progress, and whether authors evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n4. **Relevance**: Whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, whether evaluated in simulation or real robots, and if the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\n5. **Limitations**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about the numerical rating scale used in the review form.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"7960595f-17d0-4e4a-abc9-6b83a463d563","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:18:44.565Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines review form questions rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JNASXJiGnEm1yZPmhMmh7c","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965318/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965317/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines and review form questions:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of the work.\n\nThe specific review form questions include:\n\n1. **Originality**: Whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how the work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n2. **Quality**: Whether the submission is technically sound, claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, methods are appropriate, whether it is complete work or work in progress, and whether authors evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n3. **Clarity**: Whether the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\n4. **Relevance**: Whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, whether evaluated in simulation or real robots, and if the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\n5. **Limitations**: CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about the numerical rating scale used in the review form."],"durationSeconds":6.879958040000002}}
