{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U2xLCMCwCGbAXM9p5jU4Hv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL openreview rating scale 1-10 accept reject overall score\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3\"},{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process\"},{\"title\":\"What Have We Learned from OpenReview?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05885\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing the Machine Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.12919\"},{\"title\":\"ML Researchers Support Openness in Peer Review But Are Concerned About Resubmission Bias\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23439\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the OpenReview rating scale:\n\nThe OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 rating scale with the following descriptions:\n- 10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\n- 9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\n- 8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\n- 5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\n- 4: Ok but not good enough - rejection\n- 3: Clear rejection\n- 2: Strong rejection\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n\nThe threshold for acceptance is between scores 5-6, with 6 being marginally above and 5 being marginally below the acceptance threshold. This scale is used as the \"overall rating\" field in OpenReview reviews, and reviewers also provide separate numerical scores for soundness, presentation, contribution, and confidence.\n\nIt's worth noting that different conferences may use variations of this scale—for example, ICLR 2024 and 2025 use a discrete subset {1,3,5,6,8,10}.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"4536e5b7-c419-4418-a836-5a813fe88dd0","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:18:55.151Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL openreview rating scale 1-10 accept reject overall score","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Pd6ESHsusPykvdMy4CE6QJ","content":[{"title":"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3"},{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137"},{"title":"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process"},{"title":"What Have We Learned from OpenReview?","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05885"},{"title":"Analyzing the Machine Learning Conference Review Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2011.12919"},{"title":"ML Researchers Support Openness in Peer Review But Are Concerned About Resubmission Bias","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.23439"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the OpenReview rating scale:\n\nThe OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 rating scale with the following descriptions:\n- 10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\n- 9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\n- 8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\n- 5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\n- 4: Ok but not good enough - rejection\n- 3: Clear rejection\n- 2: Strong rejection\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n\nThe threshold for acceptance is between scores 5-6, with 6 being marginally above and 5 being marginally below the acceptance threshold. This scale is used as the \"overall rating\" field in OpenReview reviews, and reviewers also provide separate numerical scores for soundness, presentation, contribution, and confidence.\n\nIt's worth noting that different conferences may use variations of this scale—for example, ICLR 2024 and 2025 use a discrete subset {1,3,5,6,8,10}."],"durationSeconds":5.343254502999996}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EJXUm13rGJA995CYsSbYrm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I now have enough information about CoRL review criteria and the rating scale. Let me now summarize what I know:\n\n**CoRL Review Criteria:**\n- Originality/Novelty\n- Quality/Soundness\n- Clarity/Presentation\n- Significance/Relevance to robot learning\n- Limitations section required\n\n**Rating Scale (OpenReview 1-10):**\n- 10: Top 5%, seminal\n- 9: Top 15%, strong accept\n- 8: Top 50%, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n\n\n- 6: Marginally above threshold\n- 5: Marginally below threshold\n- 4: Ok but not enough, reject\n- 3: Clear rejection\n- 2: Strong rejection\n- 1: Trivial/wrong\n\nWith a historical acceptance rate around 30%, I need to set up two parallel reviewers—one focused on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—and equip them with the full paper, review context, and scoring rubric.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":54059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829},"output_tokens":11,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82fe1c25-39c0-4259-b5cc-ba16f1a4fb53","uuid":"a27cf494-e389-4de7-99a0-3a9eb0e5599a"}
